	"name": "Modern Horizons 2 Draft Booster",
	"notes": "15 cards. No token. Weights in a slot sum to 1000. Source is Collecting Modern Horizons 2 (May 21, 2021). Commons: 23 of 101 have a showcase, and that printing shows up once for every two regulars, so a common slot is 924 common / 33 sketch / 43 retro. Uncommons: 24 of 80, same 2-to-1, so 900 / 63 / 37. The extra 20 uncommons in the uncommon pool are new-to-Modern reprints with no Scryfall flag, same limit as MH3. New-to-Modern slot is 20 uncommon / 18 rare / 4 mythic of 42, rolled against the whole set, not that list. Rare slot is two copies of each of 60 rares and one of each of 20 mythics (780/130), and 9% of the time a retro or borderless printing instead (44/19/21/6 by pool size). Extended-art rares sit in borderless_rare because that is the treatment rule. One buy-a-box retro mythic is in retro_mythic. The last slot is a common, and a foil common in 1 of 3 packs. Wizards did not publish the foil rarity split, so this foil stays on the common sheet.",
